# PART 7 — QUESTIONS PAGE

Keep a separate sidebar page called **Questions**.

The question bank belongs to the subject, not to individual sections, because the participating sections of the same department and semester share the subject syllabus and common examination.

Question-bank identity should be associated with:

- Department.
- Semester.
- Subject.
- Academic context.
- Module.
- Question revision.

### Select subject

The HOD selects a subject created through Setup Class.

The system must dynamically load its module count and details.

Do not hardcode five modules.

### Question upload methods

Support:

1. Add an individual question manually.
2. Bulk upload through Excel.
3. PDF-to-Excel conversion followed by manual Excel upload.

### Standard question Excel template

Use these columns:

1. Module Number.
2. Question Text.
3. Option A.
4. Option B.
5. Option C.
6. Option D.
7. Correct Option.

Do not include a difficulty column.

All questions are assumed to be at the same difficulty level for this system. Do not create Easy, Medium or Hard classification.

### Module-wise question pool

Allow the HOD to:
- Select which modules to upload.
- Upload a flexible number of questions for each selected module.
- Add questions individually.
- View existing questions by module.
- Edit questions before publication.
- Remove or archive questions before publication, subject to dependency rules.

Validate:
- Required fields.
- Four distinct options.
- Valid correct answer.
- Valid module number.
- Module number within the configured subject module count.
- Duplicate question text.
- Duplicate identifiers.
- Sufficient available questions for the requested paper configuration.

Use a stable Question ID for each question. The same Question ID must remain traceable across paper versions and examination records.

### Final examination question distribution

HOD configures:
- Final paper question count.
- Module-wise question distribution.

The interface may suggest an even distribution, but the HOD must be able to adjust it.

For example, if the final paper contains 30 questions, the HOD must be able to define how many questions come from each module.

Do not fix:
- 300 total questions.
- 60 questions per module.
- Five modules.
- Any other obsolete fixed count.

### Numbered question sets

The backend generates numbered Sets 1, 2, 3 and 4 based on the HOD's configured question count and module-wise distribution.

All four numbered sets must follow the same configured paper blueprint and question count.

The HOD must be able to preview the generated sets.

The HOD explicitly clicks **Publish** to publish the sets.

Only after successful publication should they be available to the COE.

The HOD should see useful publication status, revision history and publication timestamps.

### Question-set integrity

Do not fabricate questions or silently duplicate questions to fill a set.

If the requested set generation requires more unique questions than are available, display an accurate shortage report and prevent invalid publication.

If the institution configures the four numbered sets to be fully disjoint, four N-question sets require at least 4N valid unique questions for the selected distribution.

Do not silently assume or invent an overlap policy. Follow an existing institutional/backend policy if one is configured. Otherwise, report the availability clearly and make the policy explicit in the backend contract.

### A–D shuffled versions

When the COE selects a numbered set for an examination sitting, the backend generates A, B, C and D versions for that sitting.

The versions contain the same selected questions, but question order and answer-option order are shuffled.

Stable Question IDs must be retained so that student responses and answer-key corrections can be evaluated correctly.

Do not generate A–D versions automatically during HOD publication.

### Question upload implementation

Use a real XLSX parser for Excel uploads.

For PDF-to-Excel conversion, use the same review-and-manual-upload workflow described in Setup Class.

Remove all old fake question generator functionality, especially:
- Artificial generation of questions to fill a 300-question bank.
- Fake `FILL_ALL_MODULES_TO_300` logic.
- Silent fallback to generated sample questions when file parsing fails.
- Any fake success message after an unsuccessful upload.

If parsing fails, show the real error. Never pretend the file was imported.

### Publication history

Preserve the complete question publication/revision history inside the Questions page.

Do not create a separate Submission History page.

Published revisions must remain traceable. Changes after publication should create an appropriately governed new revision, not silently modify historical examination material.

